# Racinglazing ForumService — MVP API Contract## 1. Service boundaries### ForumService owns```textCategoryForumThreadCommentVoteTagReportForum-specific moderationRaceId referenceUserId references```### UserService owns```textUserAuthenticationUser credentialsUser profileUser roles / identity```ForumService should only store:```textAuthorId```and use UserService when user information is required.### RaceService owns```textRaceDriverTeamCircuitRace resultsChampionship data```ForumService only stores:```textRaceId```when a thread is associated with a race.### Blob StorageThe actual images/videos are stored in Blob Storage.ForumService only maintains references/metadata if media is included in a thread/comment.---# 2. API conventionsBase URL:```http/api/v1```Authentication:```httpAuthorization: Bearer <token>```The API Gateway is responsible for routing/authentication concerns where applicable. ForumService should still authorize operations based on the authenticated user identity/claims.---# 3. Common response format### Single resource```json{  "data": {    ...  }}```### Collection```json{  "data": [],  "pagination": {    "nextCursor": "cursor-value",    "hasMore": true  }}```### Error```json{  "error": {    "code": "THREAD_NOT_FOUND",    "message": "The requested thread was not found."  }}```---# 4. CATEGORY APIsCategories are the highest-level grouping.Example:```textFormula 1MotoGPWECIndyCarNASCARGeneral Motorsport```Categories are primarily administrative/configuration data. For the MVP, users only need to read them.---## GET /api/v1/categoriesReturns all active categories.### Response```json{  "data": [    {      "id": "cat-001",      "name": "Formula 1",      "slug": "formula-1",      "description": "Formula 1 discussions",      "displayOrder": 1,      "forumCount": 5,      "threadCount": 12540    },    {    